  <data name="Consent_BenchTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Tune BetterRecall for this PC?</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_Intro.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>BetterRecall keeps a searchable history of what you see and hear on this PC. Nothing is captured until you agree.</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_Limit.Message" xml:space="preserve"><value>Windows Hello unlock protects your history from disk theft and from other accounts. It cannot protect it from malware running as you while you are signed in.</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_Limit.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>The limit</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_NotNow.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Not now</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_Protect1.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>• Password managers, remote desktop, sign-in and UAC screens, and private browser windows.</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_Protect2.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>• Explicit images are filtered out before indexing. BetterRecall's own windows are hidden from capture.</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_ProtectTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>What is never captured</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Before BetterRecall starts</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_What1.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>• A screen image (keyframe) about every 2 seconds while the screen changes, with the window title and app name.</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_What2.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>• The last 2 minutes of screen video and desktop audio, in memory only. It reaches disk only when you save a replay.</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_What3.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>• Audio transcripts, only if you turn on system audio or the microphone in Settings.</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_What4.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>• No text recognition (OCR). Screen images are searched by an AI model that runs on this PC.</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_WhatTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>What is captured</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_Where1.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>• Only on this PC, in your user profile (%LOCALAPPDATA%\BetterRecall), encrypted with a key protected by the TPM, a passphrase or Windows.</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_Where2.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>• Kept for 30 days by default. You can delete a time range, an app, or everything at any time.</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_Where3.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>• BetterRecall makes no network connections.</value></data>
  <data name="Consent_WhereTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Where it is stored</value></data>
